# =============================================================================
# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next Q8_0 at 131072 + MTP self-speculative decoding
# =============================================================================
# The served Q8_0 profile (qwen38-flash-next-q8-128k.env -- read it for the
# placement) with the model's own multi-token-prediction head drafting three
# tokens ahead. RESULTS 54.
#
# THE HEAD IS A SEPARATE FILE. The lmstudio-community GGUF carries no NextN
# block; the head comes from dzannotti's export, a predictor-only GGUF that
# upstream #2369 accepts via -md (one full qwen4exp block, 4 B params, its own
# token embeddings and LM head -- so it does not need the still-open #2403):
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.lmstudio/models/dzannotti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-GGUF
#   curl -L -o ~/.lmstudio/models/dzannotti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-GGUF/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-Q4_K_M.gguf \
#     https://huggingface.co/dzannotti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-GGUF/resolve/main/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-Q4_K_M.gguf
#   (2 622 313 344 bytes, sha256 1f2a6991237d5412c9582b654e89e3aaa5a0fd33206d2b6d1813b15c475f4c02)
#
# NEEDS ik_llama.cpp >= 1b542a42 (#2412, merged 2026-09-14): per-step recurrent
# checkpoints for qwen4exp. Before it, a rejected draft rolled back the whole
# slot ("gpu-fallback") and prose ran 14 % SLOWER than without MTP; with it,
# 11-14 % faster. The load log must say
#   llama_spec_ckpt_init: fixed recurrent checkpoint mode = per-step
#
# --- MEASURED 2026-09-14, d5f53d9f, 500 W, against qwen38-flash-next-q8-128k --
#
# Shallow -- 37-86-token prompts, 400 generated, so under 500 tokens of context;
# temperature 0 / 0.7 (t/s; acceptance at temperature 0):
#
#                     no MTP          MTP             accepted drafts
#   code              39.2 / 39.7     63.4 / 64.4     91 %
#   JSON extraction   39.5 / 39.7     65.9 / 67.8     94 %
#   prose             39.8 / 40.1     45.6 / 44.5     67 %
#
# Real text at depth (repo docs + source, temperature 0.7):
#
#   depth    prefill          code tg          prose tg
#   32k      1452 -> 1230     35.8 -> 52.9     36.1 -> 39.2
#   96k      1275 -> 1112     32.9 -> 38.1     32.7 -> 31.0
#   124k     1194 -> 1046     32.0 -> 36.8     32.1 -> 27.7
#
# THREE COSTS, all real:
#   * prefill -12 to -15 % at every depth. Two things contribute and they were
#     not separated: one expert layer fewer on the card (-ncmoe 18, below) and
#     the head filling its own KV as the prompt goes in.
#   * the gain fades with depth. The target verifies a draft as a 4-token batch,
#     and upstream #2404's gather -- what keeps plain decode nearly flat with
#     depth -- engages only for single-token graphs. So verification attends
#     over the whole cache again, and past ~96k prose is slower than no MTP.
#   * VRAM: 96 844 MiB peak at 124k of 97 887. It held, with ~1 GiB to spare.
#
# Output at temperature 0 is not bit-identical to the non-MTP profile -- the
# verify batch runs different kernels than single-token decode, so near-ties can
# resolve differently. That is normal for speculative decoding here, not a fault.
#
#   ./serve.sh qwen38-flash-next-q8-128k-mtp
#   ./serve-qwen38-flash-next-q8-128k-mtp.sh
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

: "${IK_MODEL_GLOB:=${IK_MODELS_ROOT}/lmstudio-community/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Q8_0-00001-of-*.gguf}"

: "${IK_ALIAS:=qwen38-flash-next-q8-128k-mtp}"
: "${IK_CTX:=131072}"

: "${IK_RTR:=0}"
: "${IK_FIT:=0}"

# 18, not the Q8 profile's 17: the head (2.1 GiB), its KV (136 MiB), its compute
# buffer (2.1 GiB) and the per-step checkpoint buffers have to fit beside the
# target. One expert layer on the host is ~3 % of plain generation; MTP pays it
# back several times over on code and JSON.
: "${IK_NCMOE:=18}"

: "${IK_UBATCH:=2048}"
: "${IK_BATCH:=2048}"

: "${IK_CTK:=q8_0}"
: "${IK_CTV:=q8_0}"

: "${IK_THREADS:=8}"
: "${IK_THREADS_BATCH:=24}"

# The draft head, fully on the GPU, with a context as long as the target's (the
# head attends over the same history). n_max=3 drafts three tokens; p_min=0.75
# stops drafting when the head is unsure -- at p_min=0 prose fell to 27 t/s
# (RESULTS 54). Q4_K_M head: its author measured a Q8_0 head agreeing with a
# quantized target LESS often; not re-checked against this Q8_0 target.
: "${IK_MTP_DRAFT:=${IK_MODELS_ROOT}/dzannotti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-GGUF/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MTP-Q4_K_M.gguf}"
: "${IK_EXTRA_ARGS:=-md ${IK_MTP_DRAFT} -ngld 99 -cd 131072 -ctkd q8_0 -ctvd q8_0 --spec-type mtp:n_max=3,p_min=0.75}"
